hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3466","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Cursing a Muslim is immorality, and fighting him is blasphemy.” I said to Abu Wael: Did you hear it from Abdullah? He said: Yes"
"3467","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Muawiyah, who is Ibn Hisham, told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Insulting a Muslim is immorality, and fighting him is disbelief.”"
"3468","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Abdullah said: “Cursing a Muslim is immoral.” And fighting him is blasphemy.”"
"3469","Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said, “Fighting a believer is blasphemy, and his insults are blasphemy.” \immorality\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"3470","Bishr bin Hilal Al-Basri told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, on the authority of Ziyad bin Riyah. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever abandons obedience and separates from the community and dies, dies the death of ignorance, and whoever He goes out against my nation, attacking its righteous, and the immoral one does not avoid its believer, nor fulfill his covenant with it, then he is not of me, and whoever fights under a blind banner calls to fanaticism, or he gets angry due to fanaticism and is killed, and he is a ignorant killer.”"
"3471","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Imran Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Jundub. Ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fights under a blind flag fights a faction and gets angry for a faction and I kill him.” Pre-Islamic times.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Imran al-Qattan is not strong. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3472","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Mansour told me, he said: I heard Rabi’i narrating, On the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a Muslim points weapons at his Muslim brother, then they are both on the edge of Hell.” And when he kills him, they all fall down therein.”"
"3473","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ali told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: “If two Muslim men take up arms against each other, they will be on the precipice of Hell. If one of them kills the other, they will be in Hell.”"
"3474","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If two Muslims confront each other with their swords and one of them kills his companion, then they will be in Hell.” It was said: O Messenger of God, this is the killer. What is the matter with the murdered person? He said: “He wanted to kill his friend.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3475","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If two Muslims confront each other with their swords and one of them kills his companion, then they will be in Hell.” The same as him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3476","Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali Al-Masisi Al-Qadi informed us, saying: Khalaf told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Tomorrow, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “When two Muslims confront each other with their swords, each one of them wanting to kill his friend, then they are in Fire.” He was told: O Messenger of God, this is the killer, so what is the matter with the killed person? He said: “He was keen to kill his friend.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3477","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Al-Khalil bin Omar bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Qatada told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan On the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If two Muslims meet with their swords and one of them kills his friend, then the killer And the one who is killed will be in the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3478","Ahmad bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Bakra, said: He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If two Muslims confront each other with their swords So one of them killed his friend, so the killer and the killed will be in the Fire. They said: O Messenger of God, this is the killer, so what is the matter with the killed? He said: “He wanted to kill his brother.”"
"3479","Ahmad ibn Abdah informed us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ayyub, Yunus, and Al-Mu’alla ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, on the authority of Abu Tomorrow, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If two Muslims meet with their swords and one of them kills his companion, then the killer and the killed In the fire"
"3480","Mujahid bin Musa told us, he said: Ismail, who is Ibn Ulayya, told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If two Muslims confront each other with their swords and one of them kills his friend, then both the killer and the killed will be in Hell.” A man said: O Messenger of God, this is the killer, so what is the matter with the killed person? He said: “He wanted to kill his friend.”"
"3481","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Waqid bin Muhammad bin Zaid, that he heard his father speaking, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Do not return to being infidels after me, by striking the necks of some of you.” \some\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"3482","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ told us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not return to being infidels after me, striking the necks of one another. The man will not be taken.” For his father’s crime, nor for his brother’s crime.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3483","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Ahmad bin Yunus told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, On the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not return to being infidels after me, striking the necks of one another, nor A man will be taken for the transgression of his father, not for the transgression of his brother.”"
"3484","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “I will not find you returning as infidels after me, striking the necks of one another. A man will not be taken for the crime of his father, nor for the crime of his brother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3485","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Ali told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Do not return to being infidels after me,” sent."
"3486","Amr ibn Zurarah informed us, he said: Ismail informed us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Bakra, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Do not return astray after me, by striking the necks of one another.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3487","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, and Abd al-Rahman told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrik, he said: I heard Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir narrates, on the authority of Jarir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the Farewell Pilgrimage, people eavesdropped. He said: “No.” “You will return as infidels after me, striking the necks of one another.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3488","Abu Ubaidah bin Abi Al-Safar told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais, he said: I was informed that Jarir bin Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “I listen to the people,” then he said: “I will not meet you after I see you return.” After me, there will be infidels, some of you will strike the necks of one another.”"
"3489","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us about Baghdadi Mukhurami, he said: Abu Hisham, whose name is Al-Mughirah bin Salamah, told us: Al-Rabi’ bin Muslim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a speech and said: God has enjoined upon you the Hajj, and a man said: Every year? So he remained silent about it until he repeated it three times, then he said: If I had said: Yes, it would have been obligatory, even if It is obligatory as you have done it. Leave me as long as I have left you, for those who were before you perished only because of their many questions and their disagreement over their prophets. “So if I command you to do something, then take it as much as you are able, and if I forbid you to do something, avoid it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3490","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi narrated, saying: Saeed bin Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Salamah narrated, saying: Abd al-Jalil ibn Humayd narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Sinan al-Du’ali, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He stood up and said: God has prescribed the Hajj for you. Al-Aqra’ bin Habis al-Tamimi said: Every year, O Messenger of God. He remained silent, so he said: If I said yes If it were obligatory, then you would neither hear nor obey, but it is one proof.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3491","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani reported, saying: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard al-Nu’man ibn Salem, saying: I heard Amr bin Aws, speaking, on the authority of Abu Razin, that he said: “O Messenger of God, my father is an old man and cannot perform Hajj, Umrah, or Al-Dhaan, he said: So perform Hajj on behalf of your father and perform Umrah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3492","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Basri informed us, he said: Suwayd, who is Ibn Amr Al-Kalbi, informed Kufi, he said: Zuhayr, who is Ibn Muawiyah Al-Jazari, he said: Suhail told us, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ An accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise, and one Umrah to another is an expiation for what came between them.”"
"3493","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i reported, saying: Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Al-Minhal Basri, told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, he said: He informed me. Suhail, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “An accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise is the same, except that, he said, it expiates what is between them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3494","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi informed us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Muammar informed us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “A man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, which deeds are best? He said: Faith.” By God, he said: Then what? He said: Then jihad in the path of God. He said: Then what? He said: Then an accepted Hajj. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3495","Issa bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Makhramah, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Suhail bin Abi Saleh, he said: I heard my father, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The delegation of God is three: the invader, the pilgrim, And the one who performs Umrah"
"3496","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam narrated, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, who said: Khaled, who is the son of Yazid, an Egyptian, narrated to us. On the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Jihad for the old, the young, the weak, and the woman: Hajj and Umrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3497","Al-Hussein bin Al-Harith Al-Maruzi reported, saying: Al-Fudayl, who is Ibn Iyaad, narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs Hajj to this House and does not commit obscenity or immorality, will return as his mother gave birth to him.”"
"3498","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahwayh reported, saying: Jarir, who is Ibn Abd al-Hamid, reported on the authority of Habib, who is Ibn Abi Amra. On the authority of Aisha bint Talha, she said: Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, told me: “I said: O Messenger of God, shall we not go out and fight with you? I do not see any action in the Qur’an better than jihad. He said: No, but the best and most beautiful jihad is Hajj to the House, an accepted Hajj."
"3499","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Umrah to Umrah is atonement for what came between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise.”"
"3500","Abu Dawud Sulaiman bin Saif Al-Harrani told us, he said: Abu Attab, who is Sahl bin Hammad, told us, he said: Ezra bin Thabit told us. On the authority of Amr bin Dinar, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Continue between Hajj and Umrah, for they are They remove sins just as a furnace removes impurities from iron.”"
"3501","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub bin Ibrahim Al-Marwazi reported, saying: Sulayman bin Hayyan Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Amr bin Qays. On the authority of Asim, who is Ibn Bahdala, on the authority of Shaqiq, who is Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Continue between Hajj and Umrah, for they remove poverty and sins just as a furnace removes impurities from iron, gold, and silver, but it is not for Hajj. “What is accepted is a reward less than Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3502","Muhammad ibn Bashhar narrated, he said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Ja`far Ghandar, narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, narrating, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “A woman vowed to perform Hajj and died, and her brother, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came.” So he asked him about that, and he said: “What do you think, if your sister owed a debt, would you have settled it?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Settle with God, for He is more deserving of repayment.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3503","Imran bin Musa Basri told us, he said: Abd al-Warith, who is Ibn Sa`id, told us: Abu al-Tayyah, whose name is Yazid bin Humaid Basri said: Musa bin Salamah al-Hudhali told me that Ibn Abbas said: “A woman ordered Sinan bin Salamah al-Juhani to... He asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that her mother died and did not perform Hajj. Is it sufficient for her mother to perform Hajj on her behalf? He said: Yes, if Her mother owed a debt and she was paying it off on her behalf. Would that not be sufficient for her? Should she perform Hajj on her mother’s behalf?"
"3504","Othman bin Abdullah bin Khurzad from Antioch told me, he said: Ali bin Hakim Al-Awdi told us, he said: Humaid bin Abd told us. Al-Rahman Al-Rawasi said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “ A woman asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about her father who died and did not perform Hajj. He said: “Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3505","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan, who is Ibn Uyaynah, told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “ A woman from Khath'am asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the morning of a gathering, and she said: O Messenger of God, what is the Hajj obligatory for His servants? I found my father was an old man who was not keen on traveling. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes. Sa`id bin Abd al-Rahman al-Makki told me. He said: Tell us. Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, the same. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3506","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Waki`, who is Ibn al-Jarrah, told us: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of al-Nu`man bin Salim, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, on the authority of Abu Razin Al-Uqaili, that he said: O Messenger of God, my father is an old man and is not able to perform Hajj, Umrah, or perform Hajj. He said: “Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and perform Umrah.”"
"3507","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Jarir, who is Ibn Abd al-Hamid, narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Yusuf bin al-Zubayr. On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, he said: “A man from Khath’am came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My father is an old man and cannot He was riding and it was God’s obligation of Hajj. Is it sufficient for me to perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: You are his eldest child. He said: Yes. He said: Have you seen if it were? He owed a debt. Did you pay it off? He said: Yes. He said: So perform Hajj on his behalf?"
"3508","Abu Asim Khushish bin Asram Al-Nasa’i narrated, on the authority of Abd al-Razzaq, he said: Muammar narrated, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrimah On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “A man said: O Messenger of God, my father died and did not perform Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: What do you think if your father were in debt? Were you his judge? He said: Yes. He said: God’s debt is more worthy."
"3509","Mujahid bin Musa Baghdadi told us, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, “ A man asked the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “My father’s Hajj has overtaken him, and he is very old and unable to stand firmly on his camel. If I force him, I fear that He dies, should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Have you seen that if he owed a debt and I paid it, would it be rewarding? He said: Yes. He said: So perform Hajj on behalf of your father? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3510","Muhammad bin Salamah reported to Abu Al-Harith Al-Maqbari, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sulaiman ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abbas, who said: “Al-Fadl ibn Abbas was the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then a woman from Khath’am came to him asking him to ask him, and Al-Fadl made him look at her and she looked at him, and the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, diverted the credit to the other part, and she said: O Messenger of God, God’s obligation of Hajj on His servants has been fulfilled. My father is an old man and is unable to stay with the departing woman. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes, and that was during the Farewell Hajj. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3511","Abu Dawud reported to Suleiman bin Saif, he said: Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Suleiman bin Yasar told him, that Ibn Abbas told him, “A woman from Khath’ham consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him, He greeted him during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and Al-Fadl bin Abbas was the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, it is God’s obligation to Performing Hajj on behalf of his servants. I found my father an old man who was not equal to the woman on his behalf. Is it sufficient for him that I perform Hajj on his behalf? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Yes. Then Al-Fadl bin Abbas began to look at her, and she was a beautiful woman. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took Al-Fadl turned his face to the other side."
"3512","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is the son of Harun, he said: Hisham told us, and he is the son of Hassan Basri. On the authority of Muhammad, who is Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Yasar, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, “He was a companion of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then a man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, my mother is old and old, and if I carried her she would not hold on, even if I tied her up for fear that I would kill her. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What do you think, if your mother had a debt, would you have paid it? He said: Yes. He said: “Perform Hajj on behalf of your mother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3513","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman, who is Ibn Mahdi, told us, saying: Sufyan, who is al-Thawri, told us, on the authority of Mansour, On the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Yusuf, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: “You are the eldest son of your father, so perform Hajj on his behalf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3514","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya, who is the son of Sa’id Al-Qattan, told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “A woman took a boy of hers to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, is this Hajj? He said: Yes, and you will be rewarded. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3515","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Marwazi reported, saying: Bishr bin Al-Sari told us, saying: Sufyan, who is Ibn Sa’id, told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “A woman lifted her boy from a howdah and said: O Messenger of God, is this a Hajj? He said: Yes, and you will be rewarded. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3516","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i informed us, saying: Abu Nu’aym, who is Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn, narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “A woman brought a boy to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Is this Hajj? He said: Yes, and you will be rewarded.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3517","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri Al-Basri narrated, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim bin Uqba narrated to us, And Al-Harith bin Miskin, I read it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed, and when he was in the spirit he met a people and said: Who are you? They said: Muslims.” They said: Who are you? He said: Messengers of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Then a woman took out a boy from the palanquin and said: Is this this? Hajj? He said: Yes, and you will be rewarded. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3518","Suleiman bin Dawud Abu Al-Rabi’ and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Malik told me Ibn Anas, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a woman who was in A boy took her with her, and she said: Is this for Hajj? He said: Yes, and you will be rewarded. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abraham, Muhammad, and Moses. Banu Uqba, they are all trustworthy, and the most narrated of them is Musa bin Uqba, and they are from the people of Medina. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3519","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: Yahya bin Saeed informed us, he said: Amra told me that she heard Aisha It says: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for the remaining five days of Dhul-Qa’dah, doing nothing but Hajj, until when we approached, meaning from Mecca. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that whoever did not have a sacrificial animal with him, when he circumambulated the Kaaba, to make it permissible.”"
"3520","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah bin Omar told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ The people of Medina will perform ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, the people of Syria from al-Juhfa, and the people of Najd from Qarn. Abdullah said: I have been informed that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The people of Yemen will perform ihram from Yalamlam."
"3521","Qutaibah bin Saeed narrated, saying: Al-Layth bin Saad narrated to us, saying: Nafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, “Indeed a man rose in The mosque, and he said: O Messenger of God, where do you order us to perform the ihram from? Al-Hulayfa, and the people of the Levant will perform ihram from Al-Juhfa, and the people of Najd will perform ihram from Qarn.” Ibn Umar said: They claim that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: The people of Yemen perform ihram from Yalamlam, and Ibn Umar used to say: I did not learn this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"3522","Amr bin Mansour informed us, he said: Hisham bin Bahram told us, he said: Al-Ma’afi, who is the son of Imran Mawsili, told us, on the authority of Aflah Bin Humaid, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed a time for the people of Medina Dhu al-Hulaifa, and for the people of Syria And Egypt is Al-Juhfa, and for the people of Iraq is Dhat Irq, and for the people of Yemen is Yalamlam.”"
"3523","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman, the companion of Al-Shafi’i, reported: Yahya bin Hassan told us: Wahib, who is Ibn Khaled Basri, told us: And Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed a time for the people of The city is Dhul-Hulaifa, and for the people of the Levant is Al-Juhfa, and for the people of Najd is Qarn, and for the people of Yemen is Yalamlam, and he said: This is for them, and for every one who comes. It comes upon them from other than them, so whoever whose family is below the miqat shall establish it until that comes upon the people of Mecca.”"
"3524","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ The people of Medina will perform ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, the people of Syria from al-Juhfa, and the people of Najd from Qarn.” It was mentioned to me, but I did not hear, that he said: The people of Yemen perform ihram from Yalamlam (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3525","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar told me, he said: Abu Hashim Muhammad bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Mu’affa, on the authority of Aflah bin Humaid, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave time to the people of Medina from Dhu al-Hulaifah and to the people of the Levant and Egypt.” Al-Juhfa, and for the people of Iraq is Dhat Irq, and for the people of Yemen is Yalamlam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3526","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi reported on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far Ghandar, who said: Muammar told us, he said: Abdullah bin Tawoos told me On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made time for the people of Medina Dhu al-Hulayfah, and for the people of Syria Al-Juhfa, and for the people of Najd, Qarn, and for the people of Yemen, Yalamlam. He said: It is for them, and for those who come to them from among others, for those who want to perform Hajj. And Umrah, then from where it began, what will reach the people of Mecca.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3527","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, A time for the people of the city of Dhu al-Hulayfah, and for the people of the Levant al-Juhfa, and for the people of Yemen Yalamlam, and for the people of Najd Qarn, so it will be easy for them and for those who Someone from other than their family came to them, who wanted to perform Hajj and Umrah, so whoever was below them is from his family, to the point that the people of Mecca perform the ihram from her. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"3528","Issa bin Ibrahim bin Mathrud Al-Masry reported on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus, who is the son of Yazid Al-Aili, informed me, he said: He said Ibn Shihab: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar told me that his father said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spent the night in Dhu al-Hulayfah.” His principle and he prayed in her mosque.”"
"3529","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Saffar Al-Basri reported, on the authority of Suwayd, who is the son of Amr Al-Kalbi, on the authority of Zuhair, who is the son of Muawiyah, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Indeed, while he was in The wedding party in Dhul-Hulayfah was brought, and it was said to him: “Indeed, you are in Batha’a, blessed.”"
"3530","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Masry and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, consecrated the Batha’a in Dhu al-Hulaifa and prayed with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3531","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahwayh narrated, he said: Al-Nadr narrated, and he is Ibn Shumail, he said: Ash’ath narrated to us, and he is Ibn Abd. King Abu Hani, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the noon prayer in Al-Bayda, then rode He ascended Mount Al-Baida and performed Hajj and Umrah when he prayed the noon prayer.”"
"3532","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a recitation by him while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asma bint Umays, “She gave birth to Muhammad bin Abi Bakr in al-Bayda’, Abu Bakr mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Order her to wash herself and then perform her ihram prayer. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3533","Ahmad bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim Al-Nasa’i narrated, saying: Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Bilal narrated to us, he said: narrated to us Yahya, who is the son of Saeed Al-Ansari, said: I heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, narrating on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakr, “that he went out on pilgrimage with the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he performed the Farewell Pilgrimage, and with him was his wife, Asma’ bint Umays al-Khathamiyah. When they were in Dhu al-Hulayfah, Asma’ gave birth to Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, so Abu Bakr came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to He commands her to wash herself, then perform the ihram for Hajj, and to do what people do, except that she does not circumambulate the Kaaba.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3534","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas and Al-Miswar bin Makhramah said, “They disagreed with Al-Abwa’, and Ibn Abbas said that the muhrim should wash his head, and Al-Miswar said that he should not wash his head, so Ibn Abbas sent me Abbas went to Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari. I asked him about that. I found him bathing between the horns of the well, and he was covered with a garment, so I greeted him. upon him, and I said: Abdullah bin Abbas sent me to you to ask you how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wash his head while he was in Ihram. So Abu Ayyub put his hand on the garment and folded it until it appeared, meaning his head, then he said to a man to pour water on his head, then he moved his head With his hands, he approached them and turned away, and said: This is what I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing."
"3535","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Masri and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me On the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a person in ihram to wear dyed clothing.” With saffron or burrs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3536","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked what The person in ihram should wear a type of clothing. He said: He should not wear a shirt, a robe, trousers, a turban, or a garment that has been touched by rice, saffron, or “Keeps, except for one who finds sandals. If he does not find sandals, then let him cut them off until they are lower than the ankles.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3537","Nuh bin Habib Al-Qumsi told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ata told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’la bin Umayyah, on the authority of his father, said: “I wish I could see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descending upon him, while we are With the scarab while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in a dome, then the revelation came to him, so Omar indicated to me to come, so I entered the dome with my head. Then a man who had entered ihram in a jubbah for Umrah came to him, anointed with perfume, and he said: O Messenger of God, what do you say about a man who had entered ihram in a jubbah when he was revealed? The revelation came upon him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, began to sigh, so it was hidden from him, and he said: Where is the man who asked me before? So the man was brought, and he said “As for the garment, take it off, and as for the perfume, wash it off, then enter into an ihram.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: “Then enter into an ihram, I do not know.” No one said it other than Nuh bin Habib, and I do not think it has been preserved, and God Almighty knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3538","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, “A man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, What clothes should the person in ihram wear? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not wear shirts, turbans, trousers, or robes. Nor the slippers, unless someone does not find sandals, let him wear slippers, and cut them below the ankles. Do not wear anything that has been touched by saffron, nor \Al-wars\"""""""
"3539","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, and he is Ibn Saeed, he said: Ubaid Allah told us, and he is Ibn Omar, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Omar, “A man said: O Messenger of God, what clothes should we wear when we enter ihram? He said: Do not wear a shirt.” Amr once said: Other: Shirts, turbans, trousers, or socks, unless one of you has sandals, in which case he should cut them off below the ankles, or a garment. Neither rose nor saffron touched it.”"
"3540","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad, who is Ibn Zayd, told us, on the authority of Amr, who is Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, giving a sermon and he said: “Trousers are for those who cannot find a garment, and sandals are for those who cannot find sandals.” \For the forbidden\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"3541","Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan al-Ruqi told me, he said: Ismail reported, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever does not find a lower garment, let him wear trousers, and whoever does not find “Shoes, let him wear slippers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3542","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: “A man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, what Do you command us to wear certain types of clothing during the ihram? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not wear a shirt, trousers, or turbans. A hoodie, or slippers, unless someone has no sandals, in which case he should wear the slippers, which are lower than the ankles, and do not wear any “The clothes may not be touched by saffron or rose, and the woman must not cover herself forbidden things, and she must not wear gloves.”"
"3543","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, “A man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, What clothes should the person in ihram wear? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not wear shirts, turbans, trousers, or robes. And not the slippers, unless someone cannot find sandals, let him wear slippers and cut them lower than the ankles, and do not wear anything that has been touched by saffron, nor \Al-wars\"""""""
"3544","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya and Amr bin Ali Abu Hafs Al-Fallas told me, saying: Yazid, who is the son of Harun, told us. He said: Yahya, who is Ibn Saeed, reported on the authority of Omar Ibn Nafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Omar, “Indeed, a man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace be upon him, said: What clothes should we wear when we enter ihram? He said: Do not wear a shirt, trousers, turbans, robes, or slippers. Unless someone has no sandals, he should wear socks lower than the ankles, and do not wear any clothing that has been touched by roses or saffron. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Omar bin Nafi’, Abu Bakr bin Nafi’, and Abdullah bin Nafi’ are three brothers, and Abdullah bin Nafi’ is not trustworthy, and Nafi’ is the client of Abdullah bin Umar, trustworthy and a custodian. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3545","Abu Al-Ash’ath narrated to Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam, he said: Yazid narrated to us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Ayoub narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar said: “A man called to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: What should we wear when we enter ihram? He said: Do not wear a shirt or a turban. Neither trousers, nor a robe, nor socks, unless you find two sandals, and if you do not find sandals, then anything below the ankles.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3546","Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, he said: Yazid bin Zuray’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Prophet called A man, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: What should we wear when we enter ihram? He said: Do not wear shirts, turbans, robes, or trousers. Slippers, unless they are sandals. If there are no sandals, then sandals below the ankles, or clothing dyed or touched with rose or saffron. \Horse or saffron\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"3547","Hanad bin Al-Sirri reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Umar reported, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not wear shirts, trousers, turbans, robes, or slippers during Ihram.”"
"3548","Ismail bin Masoud reported, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If he does not find a lower garment, let him wear trousers, and if he does not find sandals Let him wear socks.”"
"3549","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Aoun reported, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If the muhrim does not find sandals, then he should wear socks and cut them off lower than the ankles.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3550","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd reported, saying: Abdullah, who is Ibn al-Mubarak, reported on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, “A man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, what clothing do you command us to wear in the state of Ihram?” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: Do not wear shirts, trousers, or slippers, unless there is a man who does not have sandals, in which case he should wear the slippers lower than the ankles. “He should wear any clothing that has been touched by saffron or roses. A woman should not cover the sacred area or wear gloves.”"
"3551","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id al-Sarkhasi, trustworthy and trustworthy, reported to us, saying: Yahya, who is the son of Sa`id al-Qattan, narrated to us on the authority of Ubayd Allah, saying: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, on the authority of his sister Hafsa, who said: “I said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: What is the matter with the people? And you have not completed your Umrah? He said: I have tied my hair and tied my Hadi, so I will not perform it until I complete Hajj. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3552","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed Abu Al-Tahir Al-Masry and Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading from him while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his. On the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus, who is Ibn Yazid al-Ayli, informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: “I saw the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"3553","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad, who is Ibn Zayd, told us, on the authority of Amr, who is Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Aisha, “ “I perfumed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he entered ihram when he wanted to enter ihram, and when he entered ihram before he entered ihram with my hand.”"
"3554","Qutayba bin Saeed narrated, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I was kind to the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, for him to enter ihram before he enters ihram and for him to enter ihram before he circumambulates the Kaaba.”"
"3555","Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, and he is Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I congratulated the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, because he was in ihram.” When he entered ihram and it was permissible for him when he entered ihram.”"
"3556","Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi Abu Ubaid Allah Al-Makki reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha. She said: “I treated the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, kindly for his wife when he entered ihram and for his permission after he stoned the obstacle before he circumambulated the Kaaba.”"
"3557","Issa bin Muhammad Abu Umair bin Al-Nahhas reported, on the authority of Damra, who is Ibn Rabi’ah, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “I perfumed the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, for his permissibility, and I perfumed him for his ihram in a way that does not resemble this perfume of yours,” meaning that it is not for him. Survival (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3558","Muhammad bin Mansour narrated, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Urwa narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: I said to Aisha: “By what “What did she perfume with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace?” She said: “With the best perfume when it is forbidden or permissible.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3559","Ahmad bin Yahya bin Al-Wazir reported, saying: Shuaib bin Al-Layth reported, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Uthman. Ibn Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I used to perfume the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as well as he entered ihram.” I find"
"3560","Ahmad bin Harb Al-Tai narrated, saying: Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father On the authority of Aisha, she said: “I used to perfume the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with whatever I could, both for his prohibition and permissibility, and when he wanted to He visits the house.”"
"3561","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Hushaym, who is Ibn Bashir, narrated to us, saying: Mansour, who is Ibn Zazan, narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Al-Qasim, said: Aisha said: “I perfumed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, before he entered into ihram and on the Day of Sacrifice before To circumambulate the House with perfume containing musk.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3562","Ahmad bin Nasr Al-Naysaburi reported, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Walid reported, on the authority of Sufyan, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, he said: Ishaq informed us, he said: Sufyan, who is Al-Thawri, told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad. On the authority of Aisha, she said: “It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of musk on the head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Ihram,” and Ahmad said Ibn Nasr: And the scent of good musk was at the junction of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3563","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, saying: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Mansour, saying: Ibrahim told me: Tell me Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, said: “A flash of perfume was seen in the corners of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Ihram.”"
"3564","Muhammad ibn Qudamah Al-Masisi told me, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “It is as if I am looking at the emanation of perfume from the head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3565","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi reported, he said: Abu Dawud reported, he said: Shu’bah reported, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, said: “I was looking at the glimmer of perfume in the roots of the hair of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in ihram.”"
"3566","Humayd ibn Masada al-Basri reported, saying: Bishr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “It is as if I am looking at a stream of perfume at the junction of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it is \Forbidden\"""""""
"3567","Bishr ibn Khalid informed, he said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Ja`far, reported, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, who is Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I saw a glimmer of perfume on the head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3568","Hanad bin Al-Sari Al-Kufi reported, saying: Abu Muawiyah, who is the blind man Muhammad bin Khazim, told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad. On the authority of Aisha, she said: “It is as if I were looking at the rays of perfume in the corners of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was performing the ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3569","Qutayba bin Saeed and Hannad bin Al-Sari reported on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanted to enter ihram, he would anoint him with the best oil he could find until I could see it shining on his head and beard.” Israel followed him up on this statement, and said: On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3570","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Basri reported, saying: Yahya bin Adam reported, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I used to perfume the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with the best I could find.” Of perfume until I see the glimmer of perfume on his head and beard before he enters ihram.”"
"3571","Imran bin Yazid Al-Dimashqi told me, he said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, said: “I saw a flash of perfume at the corners of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after three days.”"
"3572","Ali ibn Hajr ibn Iyas reported, he said: Sharik reported, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I used to see And the scent of perfume was at the junction of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after three days, while he was in Ihram.”"
"3573","Humayd ibn Masada Basri narrated on the authority of Bishr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, who said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, said: “I asked Ibn Umar about perfume when entering the state of Ihram, and he said: Because being daubed with tar is more beloved to me than that. So I mentioned this to Aisha, and she said: May God have mercy on Abu Abdul Rahman. I used to perfume the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he went around. his wives, then in the morning he exudes perfume.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3574","Hanad bin Al-Sirri reported, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Mis’ar, meaning Ibn Kadam, and Sufyan, meaning Ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, On the authority of his father, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: For me to become covered in tar is more beloved to me than to become in ihram, to sprinkle perfume. So I went to Aisha, so I told her what he said, and she said: “I made the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, good, so he went around his wives and then became in ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3575","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahwayh reported, on the authority of Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a man to be saffron.”"
"3576","Kathir ibn Ubaid al-Humsi told me, on the authority of Baqiyah, meaning Ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Shu`bah. He said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhaib, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade saffron.”"
"3577","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Anas, who is Ibn Malik, “that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade saffron.” Hammad said: It means for men."
"3578","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’la, On the authority of his father, “A man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, having performed the Ihram for Umrah, wearing pieces of cloth, and he was wearing a loose garment, so he said: I perform the Ihram. Umrah, what should I do? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What did you do during your Hajj? He said: I was throwing this and washing it, so he said: What? “You were good in your Hajj, so do the same in your Umrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3579","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Ulayya told me, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: my father told us, he said: I heard Qays bin Saad, narrating on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’la, on the authority of his father, said: “A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was He was wearing a scarab, and he was wearing a robe, and he was dyeing his beard and head. He said: O Messenger of God, I entered ihram for Umrah, and I am as you can see. He said: “Take off your robe and wash your yellow robe, and whatever you did during your Hajj, do it during your Umrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3580","Qutayba bin Saeed bin Jamil bin Tarif reported, saying: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, told us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Nabih bin Wahb, on the authority of Aban bin Uthman, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “In a Muhrim, if his eyes complain He binds them up with patience.”"
"3581","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna reported on the authority of time, saying: Yahya ibn Sa`id, meaning al-Qattan, told us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ali, he said: he told me My father, he said: We came to Jabir bin Abdullah, and we asked him about the proof of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he told us that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If I had received from my affairs what I had managed to do, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal to drink and made it an Umrah. So whoever does not have a sacrificial animal should make it permissible.” And let him make an umrah for them.” And Ali came from Yemen with a gift, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought a gift from Medina, and behold, Fatima So she went in and put on dyed clothes and applied kohl. Ali said: So I went off as a hustler and asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to consult the Messenger of God. So I said: O Messenger of God. By God, Fatima wore dyed clothes and applied kohl, and said: My father commanded me to do it. He said: She spoke the truth, she spoke the truth, she spoke the truth, I commanded her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3582","Muhammad bin Bashar told me, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “A man fell from his riding mount and it crippled him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wash him with water and lotus leaves.” He will be shrouded in two garments, covering his head and face, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3583","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Basri reported, saying: Abu Dawud, meaning Al-Hafari, reported on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Saeed. Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “A man died, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wash him with water and lotus leaves, and shroud him with his clothes, and do not Cover his face and not his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection to respond.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3584","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id Abu Qudamah and Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Kawsaj al-Maruzi reported on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, who is the son of Mahdi. On the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, singled out the Hajj.”"
"3585","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “The family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the Hajj.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3586","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi Basri told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, arriving at the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever wishes to start the crescent moon for Hajj? Let him perform Ihram, and whoever wishes to perform Ihram for Umrah, let him perform Ihram for Umrah.”"
"3587","Muhammad bin Ismail al-Tabarani told me, he said: Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Hanbal told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed, meaning al-Qattan, told us, he said Shu’bah told us, he said: Mansour, meaning Ibn al-Mu’tamir, and Sulayman, meaning al-A’mash, told me, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, She said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, thinking only that it was Hajj. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3588","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh reported, saying: Jarir, meaning Ibn Abd al-Hamid, reported on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Al-Sabi bin Ma’abad said: “I was a Christian Bedouin, so I converted to Islam. I was keen on jihad, and I found Hajj and Umrah prescribed for me. So I came to a man from my tribe, his name is Hudaym bin Abdullah, and I asked him, and he said: Collect them, then slaughter whatever sacrificial animal you find. So I welcomed them, and when we came to Al-Athib, Salman bin Rabi’ah and Zayd bin Suhan met me, and I welcomed them, and one of them said to the other: What? This is one of the wisest of his camels, so I went to Omar and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I have embraced Islam and I am keen on jihad, and I have decided to perform Hajj. And Umrah was prescribed for me, so I came to Hudaym bin Abdullah and said: Oh Hana, I found Hajj and Umrah prescribed for me, and he said: Gather them together, then slaughter whatever sacrificial animal you find. So I said hello, and when I came to Al-‘Athib, I met Salman bin Rabi’ah and Zayd bin Suhan. He said: One of them said to the other: “This man is not the sharpest of his camels.” Omar said: “I have been guided by the Sunnah of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Musab bin Al-Miqdam narrated, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Shaqiq, he said: He narrated to us. The boy mentioned something similar and said: So I went to Omar and told him the story, except for his saying: Oh Hana. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3589","Imran ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi informed me. He said: Shuaib informed me, meaning Ibn Ishaq. He said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, and Abraham informed me. Ibn Al-Hasan, he said: Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj said: Hassan Ibn Muslim told me, on the authority of Mujahid and others, on the authority of a man from the people of Iraq. It is said to him: Shaqiq ibn Salamah Abu Wa’il, “A man from Banu Taghlib, called al-Sabi ibn Ma’bad, was a Christian, so he converted to Islam, and he accepted from The first time he performed Hajj, he performed the Talbiyah with both Hajj and Umrah, and he also performed the Talbiyah with both of them, so he passed by Salman bin Rabi’ah and Zayd bin Suhan, and said: One of them said: Because you are more misguided than this camel of yours. Al-Dhabi said: It remained in my mind until I met Omar ibn Al-Khattab, so I mentioned that to him, and he said: I have been guided. According to the Sunnah of your Prophet.” Shaqiq said: I and Masruq ibn al-Ajja’ used to disagree and go to al-Dhabi ibn Ma’bad to mention him, but we disagreed. Me and Masruq bin Al-Ajda' repeatedly came to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3590","Imran bin Yazid Al-Dimashqi told me, he said: Isa told us, meaning Ibn Yunus, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Marwan bin Al-Hakam, said: “I was sitting with Uthman, and he heard Ali performing Umrah and Hajj, so he said: Were you not He forbade this and said: Yes, but I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recite them both, so I did not leave the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he gave peace to your words.”"
"3591","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh reported, saying: Abu Amir, who is Al-Aqdi, reported, saying: Shu’bah told us, about the ruling, he said: : I heard Ali bin Al-Hussein, speaking on the authority of Marwan, “that Uthman forbade Mut’ah, and for a man to combine Hajj and Umrah, so he said Ali: I am here to perform Hajj and Umrah together. Uthman said: And I forbade them both. Ali said: I would not abandon the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted one of the people.” Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Al-Nadr, who is Ibn Shumail, narrated to us on the authority of Shu’bah, with this chain of narration, Like him"
"3592","Muawiyah bin Salih Abu Ubayd Allah Al-Ash’ari told me, he said: Yahya bin Ma’in told us, he said: Hajjaj, meaning the one-eyed son of Muhammad, told us, He said: Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, meaning Ibn Aazib. He said: “I was with Ali Ibn Abi Talib. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to go to Yemen. When he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Ali said: So I came to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: How did you do? I said: I declared Ihram to destroy you. He said: I drove the sacrificial animal. And I qiran, he said: And he said to his companions: If I had received from my affairs as I had managed to do, I would have done as you did, but I drove the sacrificial animal and I qiran. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3593","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani reported, saying: Khalid, meaning Ibn al-Harith, reported to us, saying: Shu’bah told us, saying: Humayd ibn Hilal told us, He said: I heard Mutarraf, saying: Imran bin Husayn told me: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined Hajj and Umrah, then he died before... He forbids it and makes it forbidden before the Qur’an is revealed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3594","Amr bin Ali told Abu Hafs Al-Fallas, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn. “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined Hajj and Umrah, and no book was revealed about them, nor did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid them.” And peace be upon them.” A man said about them whatever he wanted. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3595","Abu Dawud Sulaiman bin Saif Al-Harrani told us, he said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ismail bin Muslim told us, he said: Muhammad told us Ibn Wasi’, on the authority of Mutarrif Ibn Abdullah, who said: Imran Ibn Husayn said to me: “We had fun with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,” Abu Abdul Rahman: Ismail bin Muslim, three of them. This is one of them, and there is nothing wrong with him. Ismail bin Muslim is a sheikh who narrates on the authority of my father. Al-Tufayl has no problem with him, Ismail bin Muslim narrates on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and Al-Hasan is abandoned in hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3596","Mujahid bin Musa reported, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Yahya, Abdul Aziz, and Humaid, and Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported. He said: Hushaym reported Meaning Ibn Bashir al-Wasiti, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Suhayb, Humaid al-Tawil, and Yahya bin Abi Ishaq all reported on the authority of Anas that they heard him, saying : I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Here you are, Umrah and Hajj. Here you are, Umrah and Hajj.” Hanad bin Al-Sari Kufi informed, about... Abu Al-Ahwas, meaning Salam bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Asma, on the authority of Anas, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He responds to them"
"3597","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Durqi reported, saying: Hushaym told us, saying: Humaid Al-Taweel reported, saying: Bakr bin Abdullah reported. Al-Muzani said: I heard Anas narrating. He said: “I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting the Umrah and Hajj together,” so I narrated that. Ibn Omar, and he said: He performed Hajj alone, so I met Anas, and I told him what Ibn Omar said, and Anas said: You do not think of us as anything but boys. I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Here you go, Umrah and Hajj together.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3598","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Hujain, meaning Ibn al-Muthanna Baghdadi, told us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, that Abdullah bin Omar said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Farewell Pilgrimage.” From Umrah to Hajj and offered a sacrifice, so he brought with him the sacrifice from Dhul-Hulayfah, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began and performed the Umrah. Then the Hajj was declared, and the people enjoyed the Umrah with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until the Hajj. Among the people were those who gave a gift but did not do so. And among them were those who did not convert. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Mecca, he said to the people: Whoever among you is more guided is not permissible for anything. He is deprived of it until he completes his Hajj, and whoever is not well-guided, let him circumambulate the Kaaba, Safa, and Marwah, and shorten his Hajj, and perform Ihram, then perform Ihram. During the Hajj and then to make a sacrifice, and whoever cannot find a sacrifice, let him fast for three days during the Hajj and seven when he returns to his family. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated. May God bless him and grant him peace, when he came to Mecca, he prayed the pillar first thing, then he trotted three of the seven circumambulations and walked four circumambulations, then he bowed. When he performed two rak'ahs of circumambulation of the Kaaba at the Maqam, then said the salutation, he left and came to Safa. He circumambulated Safa and Marwah seven times, then He did not permit anything of which he had been deprived until he had completed his Hajj, sacrificed his sacrifice on the Day of Sacrifice, and departed and circumambulated the Kaaba. Then he permitted himself of everything of which he had been deprived. And he did the same as what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did, whoever offered a gift and carried the sacrificial animal from among the people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3599","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala told us, he said: I heard Saeed bin al-Musayyab, He says: “Ali and Uthman performed Hajj, and when we were on the other side of the road, Uthman forbade us from performing tamattu’. He said: If you see that he has departed, then depart, so Ali responded.” And his companions were performing Umrah, but Uthman did not forbid them. Ali said: Was I not informed that you forbid tamattu’? He said: Yes. Ali said to him: Didn’t he? Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Yes?"
"3600","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal bin Al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib, that he told him, “that he heard Saad bin Abi Waqqas and Al-Dahhak bin Qais, in the year of Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan’s Hajj, and they were They mentioned the transition from Umrah to Hajj, and Al-Dahhak said: Only one who is ignorant of the command of God does that. Saad said: What you said is miserable, my nephew. Al-Dahhak said: Omar bin Al-Khattab forbade that. Saad said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did it and we did it with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3601","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar reported, and the pronunciation for him said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Amara. Ibn Umair, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Abi Musa, “He was giving fatwa by mut’ah, and a man said to him: Have a look at some of your fatwas, for you do not know The Commander of the Faithful had not yet spoken about the rituals, until I met him and asked him, and Omar said, I knew that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had done it. “But I disliked that they should continue to celebrate their wedding with them in the desert and then go on Hajj and have their heads dripping.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3602","Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq reported, he said: My father reported, he said: Abu Hamza, who is Al-Sukkari, reported on the authority of Mutarrif, meaning Ibn Tarif, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kuhail, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard Omar saying: “By God, I am forbidding you from pleasure.” And it is in the Book of God, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did it, meaning the Umrah during Hajj. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3603","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri reported, saying: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hujayr, on the authority of Tawus, he said: Muawiyah said to Ibn Abbas: “Did you know that I shortened the head of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the Marwa?” He said: No, Ibn Abbas: This is Muawiyah’s duty to forbid people from Mut’ah, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, enjoyed Mut’ah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3604","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa al-Zaman reported on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, who said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Sa`id, told us, on the authority of Qais, On the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Batha’, and he said: “For what did you confuse me?” I said: I performed the ihram with the ihram of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Did you drink a sacrificial animal?” I said: No. He said: “So circumambulate the Ka’bah, Safa, and Marwah.” Then he came, “So I walked around the House, Safa, and Marwah, then I went to a woman from my people and she combed me and washed my head, so I was giving fatwas to the people.” Thus, during the emirate of Abu Bakr and the emirate of Omar, I was standing during the season when a man came to me and said: You do not know what has happened, Amir. The believers regarding ritual rituals, I said: O people, whoever we have given a fatwa to about something should be careful, for the Commander of the Faithful is coming to you, so complete it. With it, when he came, I said: O Commander of the Faithful, what is this that you have done regarding rituals? He said: If we follow the Book of God Almighty, then God Almighty said: And complete the Hajj and Umrah for God, and if we follow the Sunnah Our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not permissible until he slaughtered the sacrificial animal. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3605","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub Al-Jawzjani told me, he said: Othman bin Omar, meaning Ibn Faris Basri, told us, he said: Ismail bin Muslim told us. On the authority of Muhammad ibn Wasi’, on the authority of Mutarrif, meaning Ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shakhir, who said: Imran ibn Husayn said to me: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He enjoyed his enjoyment and we enjoyed with him.” Someone with his opinion said about it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3606","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed, meaning Al-Qattan, told us, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad told us, he said: My father told me He said: We came to Jabir bin Abdullah, and we asked him about the proof of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he told us that “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He stayed in Medina for nine Hajjs, then it was announced to the people that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would perform Hajj this year, so many people descended upon Medina. They were all seeking to follow the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and do what he did. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to meet five people. We remained from Dhul-Qi'dah and went out with him. Jabir said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among our supporters over him. The Qur’an was revealed while he knew. “His interpretation, and whatever he did with it, we did, so we left with no intention other than Hajj.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3607","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid, the Meccan reciter, and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a recitation to him while I was listening. The wording is from Muhammad. They said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “We left with no intention of anything other than Hajj, so when we I menstruated excessively, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me while I was crying, and said: Did I menstruate? I said: Yes, he said: This is something he wrote. God bless the daughters of Adam, so fulfill what a person in ihram does, except that you do not circumambulate the Kaaba.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3608","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani informed us, he said: Khaled, who is Ibn al-Harith, informed us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Qays ibn al-Harith informed me. Muslim, he said: I heard Tariq bin Shihab, he said: Abu Musa said: “I came from Yemen while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was at Munikh in Batha’ where He performed Hajj. He said: Did you perform Hajj? I said: Yes. He said: How did you say? He said: I said: Here you go with an Ihram like the Ihram of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he performed Hajj. In the House, and in Safa, and in Marwah, then I came to a woman, and she shook my head, and I began to give a fatwa to the people about that. He said: I said: The Commander of the Faithful is coming. upon you, so complete it. Omar said: If we follow the Book of God, then He commands us to complete it, and if we follow the Sunnah of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not come to his place until the sacrifice reached his place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3609","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa informed us of the time, saying: Yahya ibn Sa`id, meaning al-Qattan, told us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Muhammad, i.e., Ibn Ali ibn Hussein bin Ali bin Abi Talib, he said: My father told me, he said: “We came to Jabir bin Abdullah, and we asked him about the proof of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, so he told us that Ali had come from Yemen to give guidance, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought a gift from Medina. He said to Ali: What did you claim? He said: I said: Oh God, I claim what Your Messenger has claimed, and I have a sacrificial animal. He said: So do not allow it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3610","Imran bin Yazid told me, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Ata’ said: Jabir said: “Ali came from his quest, and he said to him The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: What did you declare, O Ali? He said: And Ali gave him a gift. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3611","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ja’far Tarsusi told me, he said: Yahya bin Ma’in told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, and he is one-eyed, he said: Yunus told us. Ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, he said: “I was with Ali when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to go to Yemen, so I took my guards with him.” He said: When Ali came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Ali said: I found Fatima had cleaned the house with fresh water. He said: So I passed it. She said to me: What is the matter with you? The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered his companions to perform ihram. He said: I said: I declared the ihram of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him. He said: So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to me: How did you do? I said: I deserved what I claimed. He said: Indeed, I brought the sacrificial animal. \And I was compared\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"3612","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Nafi’, “Ibn Umar wanted to perform Hajj in the year Al-Hajjaj visited Ibn Al-Zubayr. It was said to him: There is a fighting among the people, and we fear that they will repel you. So he said: Indeed, in the Messenger of God, there is a good example for you, so I will set it. Just as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did. I bear witness to you that I had made it obligatory to perform Umrah. Then he left until it appeared that they were in the desert. He said : What concerns Hajj and Umrah, except one? I bear witness that I have obligated Hajj and Umrah, and he presented a gift that he had bought with a delay, then he set out to perform ihram. He did them all until he came to Mecca, and he circumambulated the Kaaba, Safa, and Marwah, and did not do more than that. He did not slaughter, did not shave, did not cut his hair, and did not cut his hair. He freed himself from something that had been forbidden to him until the Day of Sacrifice, so he slaughtered his throat and shaved, and he saw that he had completed the Tawaf of Hajj and Umrah with his first Tawaf, and he said Ibn Umar: This is what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did."
"3613","Issa bin Ibrahim bin Mathrud Al-Masry told me, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus, meaning Ibn Yazid, told me on the authority of Ibn Shihab said: Salem told me that his father said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeting him, saying: “At your command, O God, at your command. “At your Lord, you have no partner. Indeed, praise, blessings, and dominion are yours, you have no partner.” And Abdullah bin Omar used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kneel two rak’ahs before Dhu al-Hulaifah, then when it was level with it The camel is standing at the Dhul-Hulayfah Mosque. He was greeted with these words."
"3614","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam Al-Basri reported, saying: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Zaid, And Abu Bakr, the two sons of Muhammad bin Zaid, that they heard Nafi’ narrate, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that He used to say: “At your service, O God, at your service. You have no partner at your service. Indeed, praise and blessings are Yours, and dominion is Yours, and you have no partner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3615","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, who said: “Meeting the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. At your service, O God, at your service, at your service, you have no partner. Indeed, praise and blessings are yours, and dominion is yours, you have no partner.”"
"3616","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Hushaym, meaning Ibn Bashir, told us, saying: Abu Bishr reported, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar, On the authority of his father, he said: “The talbiyah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was: ‘Labbayk, Labayk, no partner. You have no partner. Indeed, praise and blessings are Yours and the dominion, you have no partner.” And Ibn Umar added to it: “I am at your service and I am happy with you, and all good is in your hands."
"3617","Ahmad bin Abdah Al-Basri reported, saying: Hammad bin Zaid reported, on the authority of Aban bin Taghlib, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: “Part of the talbiyah of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was: Here you go, O God, here you are, no A partner with you. Indeed, praise and blessings are yours.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3618","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Fadl, On the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The talbiyah of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was for your father, the God of truth.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: I do not know of anyone who attributed this hadith except Abdullah bin Al-Fadl, and Abdullah bin Al-Fadl is trustworthy, but he disagreed with him. Ismail bin Umayyah"
"3619","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abi Bakr, On the authority of Khallad ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Gabriel came to me and said to me: O Muhammad, command your companions to They raise their voices in talbiyah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3620","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abd al-Salam, meaning Ibn Harb al-Mulai, told us, on the authority of Khaseef, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led people to pray from behind.”"
"3621","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh reported, he said: Al-Nadr reported, he said: Ash’ath, meaning Ibn Abd al-Malik, reported on the authority of Al-Hasan Ibn Abi Al-Hasan Al-Basri means, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the noon prayer in Al-Bayda, then he rode and ascended Mt. Al-Baida, and he performed the Hajj and Umrah when he prayed the noon prayer.”"
"3622","Imran ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi informed me, he said: Shuaib informed me, meaning Ibn Ishaq, he said: Ibn Juraij informed me, he said: I heard Ja`far ibn Muhammad, narrating on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, “In the Hajj of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he came to Dhu al-Hulayfah, he prayed silently until he reached al-Bayda’ \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"3623","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Salim, that he heard his father saying: “These are your hands that... “You are lying about it against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not enter the family except from the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah.”"
"3624","Issa bin Ibrahim bin Mathrud Al-Masry reported, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Salem bin Abdullah told him that Abdullah bin Omar said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, riding his camel in Dhu al-Hulaifa and then performing the ihram. where you will be leveled with it, standing straight.”"
"3625","Imran ibn Yazid informed me, he said: Shuaib, who is Ibn Ishaq, informed me, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Salih ibn Ibn Ishaq informed me. Kaisan, and Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya told me, saying: Ishaq, meaning Ibn Yusuf, told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Salih Ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to tell “that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was blessed when his camel came to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3626","Muhammad ibn al-Ala’ reported to Abu Kurayb Kufa, he said: Ibn Idris reported on the authority of Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Umar, Ibn Jurayj, and Ibn Ishaq means Muhammad ibn Ishaq, and Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Ubaid ibn Jurayj, said: “I said to Ibn Umar: I saw you performing ihram when “Your she-camel sat with you.” He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform the ihram when his she-camel sat with him and set off.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3627","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam narrated on the authority of Shuaib, meaning Ibn al-Layth, who said: Al-Layth narrated, on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Jafar bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, resided for nine years without performing Hajj, then He gave the people the call for Hajj, but no one who was able to come riding or on foot remained but he came forward, so the people prepared to go out with him, even when Dhu al-Hulayfa came and Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, so she sent for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Wash yourself. “And seek a piece of clothing and then bring it to my family.” So I did. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3628","Ali ibn Hajr ibn Iyas informed us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Ja`far, informed us, he said: Ja`far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir said: “Asmaa bint Umays passed away from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, so she sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asking him: How are you doing? So he ordered her to wash and put on her clothes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3629","Qutaybah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “We came with respite with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He said hello to a single Hajj, so Aisha came with a respite in performing an Umrah, until, when she was at Saraf, she became upset, until when we came, we circumambulated the Kaaba. And in Safa and Marwah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to let whoever among us who did not have a sacrificial animal become permissible. He said: So we said: What is permissible? He said: It is completely permissible, so we entered into intercourse with the women, applied perfume, and put on our clothes, and there was only four nights between us and Arafat. Then we performed Ihram on the day of Al-Tarwiyah, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Aisha and found her crying, and said: What is the matter with you? She said: It is my matter that I have died I menstruated, and the people were permissible, but I was not permissible and I did not circumambulate the Kaaba, and the people are going for Hajj now, so he said: This is a matter that God has decreed for my daughters. Adam, wash yourself, then perform the Hajj with your family. So she did so and made the stops until, when she was pure, she circumambulated the Kaaba and Safa and Marwah, then He said: You have completed all of your Hajj and Umrah. She said: O Messenger of God, I find in myself that I did not circumambulate the Kaaba when I performed Hajj. He said: So take her, O Abdul-Rahman, and fill her with comfort. That was the night of the measles.”"
"3630","Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Masry and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading to him while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in The Farewell Hajj, so we performed the Hajj with Umrah, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, let him perform the Hajj with Umrah, then it is not permissible until all of it is permissible. So I came to Mecca while I was menstruating, and I did not circumambulate the Kaaba or between Safa and Marwah, so I complained. That was sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Lay down your hair and walk, and complete the Hajj and leave the Umrah. So I did so, and when I completed the Hajj The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me with Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr to al-Tan`im, so I performed Umrah. He said: This is the place of your Umrah. So those who had performed Ihram for Umrah circumambulated the Kaaba and between Safa and Marwah, then they came out of ihram, then they performed another circumambulation after they returned from Mina for their Hajj. As for those who combined Hajj and Umrah, they only performed one circumambulation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
